13626	{"artifactId":"LLD-613abdb351c2c738-s3","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-613abdb351c2c738-s3-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T14:51:25.438Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S003 FR001/FR002 and ac1/ac2 (another window takes over only after 10 minutes without a sign of life and once the turn's process is gone; a turn still running after a reload is picked up again) are designed by takeOver's holderGone + LEASE_TAKEOVER_MS rule and by reclaim","evidence":"DEF.md:53-54, 142-144. chat-queue-store.ts:24 `LEASE_TAKEOVER_MS = 600_000` (10 min). The LLD's takeOver needs holderGone (holder pid and CLI both gone), and for another windowKey it also needs heartbeat staleness ≥ LEASE_TAKEOVER_MS. reclaim keeps seq/cliPid, so a reloaded turn is not failed. The same-key takeover skips the wait. That departs from the HLD sc2 comment (HLD.md:111) but keeps what recoverDeadLease does today (chat-queue-worker.ts:218), and FR005 only limits 'another window'. [files: docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/DEF.md, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-worker.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"FR004/ac5 (finished messages removed, keep within bound, refuse with a note, never drop) needs no new flush code","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:430-432 deletes the row on 'done'/'detached-ended'. enqueue (386) and resendTo (367) return `refused('full', FULL_NOTE)` when `liveCount() >= QUEUE_RECORD_BOUND` and delete nothing (resend frees only its own row first). The HLD's 'flush' wording (HLD.md:46) is raised honestly in open questions. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"takeOver and reclaim are stubs returning false; recoverDeadLease reads the lease and then calls finish() in a separate transaction","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:524-530: `takeOver() { return false; }`, `reclaim() { return false; }`. chat-queue-worker.ts:213-221: `const lease = store.lease();` is a plain read outside write(), and later `store.finish(lease.seq, {kind:'failed', error:'the window closed during the turn'...})` is its own write(). That is check-then-act across transactions. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-worker.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"dispose() currently calls leave(), which deletes the presence row; the worker never marks a closed window's head","evidence":"chat-queue-worker.ts:325 `store.leave(claim);` and chat-queue-store.ts:494-497 `DELETE FROM presence WHERE window_key = ? AND pid = ?`. tick() (223-250) acknowledges only `head.windowKey === claim.windowKey` and has no rule for a head belonging to another window. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-worker.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The display half of ac3 is existing behaviour: followLiveTurn on webview ready calls turns.follow, which takes ownership when the old host pid is gone","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:795-803 `const followLiveTurn = (s) => { ... turns.follow(s, { onEvent: ...` and it is called at 881/1805/2053. turn-lifecycle.ts:467-479: `if (live.ownerHostPid !== deps.hostPid && deps.isAlive(live.ownerHostPid)) return;` and then `s.liveTurn = { ...live, ownerHostPid: deps.hostPid }` before adapter.resume. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"presenceOf and markNotDeliveredIfHead are new; the not-delivered state and its error text already exist in finish()","evidence":"There are no presenceOf or markNotDeliveredIfHead symbols in vscode-plugin/src. chat-queue-store.ts:440-441: `case 'not-delivered': UPDATE messages SET state = 'not-delivered', error = ? ... .run('its window was closed', ...)`. LIVE_HEAD (269) selects `state IN ('queued','retrying')`, as the LLD says. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"After reclaim rewrites pid, the reloaded window can heartbeat the lease with the existing heartbeat(claim); following a reclaimed lease needs new worker code because today's heartbeat loop only runs while `current` is set","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:343 and 514-515: heartbeat updates `WHERE id = 1 AND window_key = ? AND pid = ?`, so it matches once pid becomes claim.pid. chat-queue-worker.ts:150-161: `if (disposed || current === undefined) return;`, so the reclaimed-lease rule (heartbeat + per-tick isAlive(cliPid, cliStartedAt) + finish detached-ended) is new code, and the LLD describes it as a new rule. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-worker.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The interface additions (optional holderGone, presenceOf, markNotDeliveredIfHead) break no other implementer or caller; the worker's dispose is the only caller of leave()","evidence":"ChatQueueLeases is implemented only by createChatQueueStore (chat-queue-store.ts:271). The tests use the real store (chat-queue-worker.test.ts:37, chat-queue-outbox-host.test.ts:55) or Object.create(real) wrappers, not hand-written fakes. `.leave(` has a single call site, chat-queue-worker.ts:325. takeOver/reclaim/windowAlive have no callers outside the store and test line 151. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-queue-worker.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-queue-outbox-host.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test inventory names the existing tests whose assertions change: line 151 'presence removed' and the 97df9bf7 recovery test","evidence":"chat-queue-worker.test.ts:151 `assert.equal(storeB.windowAlive('w-A', t.now()), false, 'presence removed')` is listed for inversion. The recovery test (279-322) asserts at 301 that the reloaded window's message 'one' ends `failed` after its live CLI exits. Under the LLD's reclaimed-lease rule it ends detached-ended (row deleted), so that leg must change. The LLD covers this in migration step 2 ('move the 97df9bf7 worker recovery test onto the new calls') and in the edge-case table. The builder should note that this is a flip from failed to detached-ended, not just a move. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-queue-worker.test.ts]","action":"When moving the recovery test, change line 301's expectation for the reload-with-live-CLI leg from 'failed' to the row being removed (detached-ended).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No schema change: the lease and presence columns the design needs (pid, pid_started_at, cli_pid, cli_started_at, heartbeat_at) already exist and schema stays 2","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:204-217 already defines lease (window_key, pid, pid_started_at, seq, cli_pid, cli_started_at, heartbeat_at) and presence (window_key, pid, pid_started_at, heartbeat_at). The S002 migration handles version<2 (319-321). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Once dispose stops calling leave(), presence rows 'age out' and older-plugin windows are handled","evidence":"windowAlive (532-535) treats a row older than PRESENCE_GRACE_MS as not alive, so in effect it ages out. Mixed versions are covered: an old-plugin dispose still deletes its row, and the 'no row AND message older than PRESENCE_GRACE_MS' rule handles that. The rows themselves are never deleted, though. No pruning exists in the store, and the edge-case row's 'or it was pruned' refers to nothing. The presence table keeps one stale row per window key ever seen. That is bounded by the number of workspaces, so it is harmless, but the wording overstates it. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts]","action":"Optional: change 'or it was pruned' to state that stale presence rows stay (or add a prune of rows older than LEASE_TAKEOVER_MS in presence()).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Filling takeOver/reclaim and adding to sc2/sc4 is S003's designated work, not a redesign of S001's contracts","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:135-138 comments: 'Story S003 gives the rule; until then a held lease is never taken over' and 'Story S003 gives the rule; until then a reloaded window does not reclaim'. chat-queue-worker.ts:329 'until its heartbeat times out (Story S003 takes it over)'. HLD.md:90 marks sc2 as consumed by s3. The additive presenceOf/holderGone and the change to dispose's leave() are disclosed as open questions for the sc2/sc4 owner. No S002 (outbox UI), S004 (retry classification) or S005 (review-pane) surface is touched. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-worker.ts, docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Races (two takeOvers, not-delivered vs acknowledge) are detectable because each store rule runs in one BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction that re-reads the row; StoreBusy is caught by the tick","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:283-304 write() runs `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, rolls back on throw and maps busy errors to StoreBusy. acknowledge (404-423) re-reads LIVE_HEAD and the lease in-transaction, so a guarded markNotDeliveredIfHead with the same pattern serialises against it. chat-queue-worker.ts:246-248 tick's catch logs and retries on the next poll. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-worker.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"pid reuse can only make a dead holder look alive (delay), never a live holder look gone","evidence":"chat-queue-setup.ts:63-64 `isAlive(pid) && (startedAt === undefined || startTimeOf(pid) === startedAt)`. With no start time recorded (extension.ts:603 sets it only when defaultProcessStartTime returns a value), a reused pid reads alive, so recovery is delayed. The same holds for the closed-window rule's presence pid check: a reused pid delays the not-delivered marking and never marks a live window. The LLD states this only for leases. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-setup.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"Optional: extend the pid-reuse error case to the closed-window rule (a reused presence pid delays marking the head).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of S003 ac1-ac5 maps to at least one runnable test","evidence":"The acceptance mapping covers ac1 (takeOver after LEASE_TAKEOVER_MS, B frees A's lease), ac2 (a heartbeating holder is never taken; holderGone false refuses), ac3 (reclaim keeps seq/cliPid, a reloaded window with a live CLI is not failed, detached-ended on CLI exit, plus a smoke check for the display half), ac4 (markNotDeliveredIfHead, closed-window unit test, slow-reload trade-off) and ac5 (enqueue/resendFrom at the bound). The fixtures exist: fakeTime, gatedRunner and repo() in chat-queue-worker.test.ts, and the existing bound test at chat-queue-store.test.ts:93-96. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-queue-worker.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-queue-store.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-14T14:51:25.438Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
